{"method":"initialize","params":{"protocolVersion":"2024-11-05","capabilities":{},"clientInfo":{"name":"terminal-receipts-e2e","version":"1"}},"elapsed_seconds":0.061327314004302025,"response":{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"result":{"protocolVersion":"2024-11-05","capabilities":{"logging":{},"tools":{"listChanged":true}},"serverInfo":{"name":"kwin-mcp","version":"0.1.2"},"instructions":"KDE Wayland automation in an isolated desktop. Call session_start to create it; pass session_id to later tools. Call session_stop when finished. Flow: session_start → launch_app → screenshot → mouse_click / keyboard_type / keyboard_key → screenshot to verify. Prefer find_ui_elements for named controls, accessibility_tree for structure, and screenshots if either is empty or costly. If an app is missing, use window_list and window_activate. Work without a viewer by default. When the user must see or act (password, OTP, Duo, CAPTCHA, choice, result), put the relevant entry on screen, then call viewer_open; never assume it is open or stop the session for this step. You can poll screenshots without ending your turn. Continue when the page advances. The viewer can stay open; the user can close it. Clipboards are separate. In the local viewer, Ctrl+C or Ctrl+X copies to the host; Ctrl+V or Shift+Insert pastes from the host. Use clipboard_write target=host for user paste through the viewer, target=session for agent input. Session writes also populate PRIMARY for X11 clients such as XTerm that use Shift+Insert by default. clipboard_read reads session text only. generate_secret values are withheld. At a browser login, click the field and choose saved credentials without reading or typing the value. Otherwise open the viewer. Chrome file chooser: click the file input, ctrl+l, type the absolute path, alt+o (Enter in the location bar cancels). Mouse and screenshot coordinates are pixels relative to the active window's top-left, 1:1. A cropped screenshot reports region=[x1,y1,x2,y2]; its pixel (px,py) is mouse position (px+x1,py+y1). The virtual display defaults to 1232x924; session_start accepts optional width/height to override it for that session. Windows are auto-maximized unless session_start sets window_mode=native. Input and screenshot results warn (memory_warning) when session memory is throttled. Each session_start creates a new isolated desktop. Pass only session IDs returned by your own session_start calls. A request for an ID owned by another live kwin-mcp process on this host is forwarded over a private Unix socket after checking the owner PID and effective UID; session_list remains process-local. After the owner exits or a server restart destroys its session, an old handle cannot be resumed; its unavailable-handle error includes session_status and the recorded end time and reason when available, otherwise says cleanup is unconfirmed. session_stop clears dead, stopped, expired, and start_blocked handles. Start a new session and relaunch the applications."}}}
